## No Python interop

This workspace is pure Rust: no pyo3, no embedded interpreter, no wheel, no `.pyi` stub. Nothing
links libpython, and no Rust code imports a Python package.

The Python that is here is tooling, not interop:

- `scripts/` - toolchain helpers (MSRV check, toolchain bump), covered by pytest
- `pyproject.toml` - the `dev` group plus ruff/ty/pytest configuration. It has no
  `[build-system]`: this is not a Python distribution, so uv installs those packages without
  trying to build the project.

Rules that matter when editing it:

- Logic lives in `crates/core`, written against traits. A trait with a pure-Rust implementation
  keeps the core testable; put logic there, not in the layers around it.
- Do not add pyo3 here. No crate links libpython, and nothing in the workspace is built to host
  an interpreter.
- Do not add first-party `.py` files. Python in this repo means the helpers in `scripts/`.
{%- if cookiecutter.crate_type != 'lib' %}
- `crates/cli` stays a thin binary (`clap`, `tracing`). Logic does not live there.
{%- endif %}
